umbines                                    (Ranunculaceae: <italic>Aquilegia</italic>).</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Givnish</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sytsma</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Molecular evolution and adaptive radiation</source><publisher-loc>New York, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><fpage>391</fpage><lpage>405</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006362-MacArthur1"><label>6</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacArthur</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name></person-group><year>1967</year><article-title>The theory of island biogeography.</article-title><publisher-loc>Princeton, New Jersey</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Princeton University Press</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006362-Baldwin2"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Francisco-Ortega</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>S-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sang</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Molecular phylogenetics insights on the origin and                                    evolution of oceanic islands plants.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Soltis</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Soltis</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyle</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Molecular systematics of plants II DNA sequencing</source><